Stare into the pit, pitch-black like a vinyl spin;
Echoes run laps, kick drum with a primal din;
Ropes of thought unravel, knuckles raw against the rim;
Courage on the metronome, shaking but I press begin;
Abyss got a mouth, whispers "jump"—I answer, "learn to swim."

***
It’s a long drop; clock stops; silence plays the lead;
Stars turn to ash when you're falling at that speed;
Gravity’s a poet with a lowercase creed;
Writes me in freefall, punctuates with need;
I turn fear to cadence, let the heartbeat bleed.

***
Met my shadow there, traded secrets in the fog;
Past lives on the reverb, howlin' through the bog;
Regret tried to shackle me—I outpaced it on the jog;
Built a throne from pressure, diamonds out the smog;
Found a spark in the vacuum, lit the dark into dialogue.

***
So I rise from the hush with a night-sky brim;
Carry midnight in my lungs, but my eyes stay bright, not dim;
Turn the chasm to a chapel where the basslines hymn;
Every step on the edge is a vow: I won't give in;
If you fear the abyss, make the beat your limb.

